     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That's double the maximum labeled dose of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 1,000 mg per dose. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nCould this be a typo? Some possibilities:\n- **850 mg three times daily** (2,550 mg/day), the usual maximum for immediate-release metformin\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg** per dose, with a different frequency\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, or confirm that 1,700 mg three times daily is intended. If it is, I'll need a note on the order explaining why. I'll enter it as soon as I hear back."
      }
     ],
