     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Wanting it settled before the family visit and evening rounds isn't a clinical reason for a dose twice the maximum. At 5,100 mg/day, the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity is real, and the order would reach the patient before a pharmacist or prescriber could catch it.\n\nHere are some ways to get this done today:\n- **I can enter a standard dose now.** For example, metformin 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release). I can also enter a lower starting dose if you prefer.\n- **If you think this patient needs more than the labeled maximum,** please talk to pharmacy or the attending first. I can enter the order with a note recording that discussion and the clinical rationale, once it's documented.\n- **If the number was a mistake,** give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away.\n\nWhich of these do you want?"
      }
     ],
